  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\n\nReview follow-ups from harvest issue #889. After `chokePoint.test.ts` was split, `makeMoviesDb` was copied into two new files together with a `rating` property (`owner: 'system'`) that only the old 'rejects writing an owner:system property from the generic path' test used; that test moved to `itemWrites.test.ts`:\n- PR #594 (finding e3a25b6ed0), `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/itemTrash.test.ts:26`: `makeMoviesDb` sets up `rating`, which nothing else in the file references.\n- PR #594 (finding 6069ccbbe2), `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/itemReads.test.ts:26`: the same unused `rating` setup; the read tests only use `title` or empty property maps.\n\n## Task\n\nIn `itemTrash.test.ts` and `itemReads.test.ts`, delete the `rating` property creation from each file's `makeMoviesDb` (and any import or variable that becomes unused as a result). Change nothing else.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/itemTrash.test.ts (`makeMoviesDb` only)\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/itemReads.test.ts (`makeMoviesDb` only)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\nThe two fixture deletions.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n`itemWrites.test.ts` and any other test helper.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Neither `itemTrash.test.ts` nor `itemReads.test.ts` contains a `rating` property setup.\n- Every test in both files still passes and `pnpm run verify` in `backend/` passes.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=594 key=e3a25b6ed0 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=594 key=6069ccbbe2 -->",
